    "The earlier 0.5300 and 0.5175 values are labeled combined_score. Their equivalence to the pinned macro validation HR@10, matched checkpoint selection, and per-category results are unverified; they cannot establish that aggregation caused a regression.",
    "The correction retains the deepest state, and adaptive weights depend on all depths. Even a shallow contribution can therefore depend on the deepest receptive field through its weight. This preserves causality but does not establish shorter-context selection or forgetting.",
    "Zero alpha preserves baseline outputs only if all surrounding operations remain unchanged. Adding internal padding masks could alter the supplied baseline independently. Initialization equivalence, future-token perturbation, gradient flow, and saved-predictor score parity need explicit checks.",
    "The experiment remains underspecified: actual remaining GPU budget, inherited hyperparameters, checkpoint schedule, stopping rules, and practical improvement threshold are missing. Research progress of 20% does not establish remaining compute.",
    "Baseline/static/adaptive comparisons omit a fixed-uniform correction that could distinguish depth aggregation from learned weighting. Static mode also registers unused gate_weight parameters. Report alpha, correction-to-final feature norms, and gate-replacement interventions before attributing gains to adaptive selection.",
    "Originality 4 is plausible but lacks comparison with closely related depth aggregation and zero-initialized residual methods. Difficulty 3 describes the isolated module; complete baseline integration, diagnostic adaptation, and predictor consistency remain more demanding. Potential 7 is a hypothesis, with no new validation evidence or protection against item-identity/popularity shortcuts."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Establish the closest prior art and assess whether the proposed combination contributes beyond existing depth mixing and residual initialization methods.",
      "query": "Compare NextItNet SkipRec adaptive depth recommendation, Jumping Knowledge Networks, ELMo learned scalar layer mixing, and ReZero zero-initialized residual connections with a causal positionwise softmax over channel-normalized residual depths whose differences from the final state are added through a zero-initialized scalar. What architectural distinctions and ablation controls are supported by these papers?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Clarify the mechanism: same-position causal aggregation can still use distant context through both the final residual path and the gate.",
      "query": "In causal dilated convolution networks, when adaptive layer aggregation weights depend on the deepest hidden state and the output retains a direct deepest-state residual path, can shallow-layer weighting reduce dependence on old inputs? Find methods for measuring effective receptive fields and matched prefix-perturbation or gate-replacement interventions that distinguish context suppression from feature reweighting."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Improve the evaluation plan without changing the pinned evaluator or introducing additional independently trained predictors at deployment.",
      "query": "For sequential recommendation evaluated with 200 validation users per dataset, one positive and 99 sampled negatives, what do sampled-ranking evaluation and adaptive validation selection studies recommend for comparing small HR@10 differences? Address paired user-level uncertainty, repeated checkpoint selection, fixed candidate sets, and limits on extrapolating sampled HR@10 to full-catalog recommendation quality."
    }
  ]
